# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Cloudflare Pages — redirects & routing rules
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/
#
# Astro static output generates real index.html files for every route, so
# SPA-style catch-all is NOT needed. Direct navigation works out of the box.
#
# This file handles:
#   1. Trailing-slash normalisation (canonical URLs)
#   2. Legacy / renamed route redirects
#   3. 404 fallback (CF Pages picks up /404.html automatically)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Trailing slash normalisation ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Cloudflare Pages serves index.html for both /case-study and /case-study/
# by default, so explicit redirects here are only needed if you want to
# enforce one canonical form. Astro already outputs /case-study/index.html
# so both forms resolve; the canonical <link> in each page handles SEO.

# ── Legacy / renamed routes ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# If any old URL was ever shared publicly, redirect it permanently.
/index-new  /  301
/hero-demo  /  302

# ── www → apex ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Cloudflare DNS handles this via a CNAME record; no redirect rule needed here.
# But if you ever point www CNAME here directly, uncomment:
# https://www.davincistudio.ae/*  https://davincistudio.ae/:splat  301
